      "id": 1,
      "text": "Trufant was platted on March 10, 1875, and named after its first settler, Emery Trufant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trufant%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Emery Trufant built the first water‑powered sawmill in the community in 1872.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trufant%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Later, Hileman and Jacob Hesser erected a steam‑powered mill on the same site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trufant%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Trufant sits in the southeast part of Maple Valley Township in western Montcalm County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trufant%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town lies 11 miles southeast of Howard City, 15 miles northeast of Cedar Springs, and 13 miles northwest of Greenville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trufant%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Muskellunge Lake, located in Trufant’s eastern edge, drains south through a chain of lakes to the Flat River, a Grand River tributary.",
